      "source": [
        "## Dimensionality Reduction and Feature Visualization\n",
        "The BERT embeddings live in a 768-dimensional space — too high to visualize directly. We use [t-SNE](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.manifold.TSNE.html) to project both the textual and concise embeddings down to 3 dimensions, preserving local structure so that samples with similar features appear close together in the plot.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 13,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "m2ke98CayZ4Y"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.manifold import TSNE\n",
        "\n",
        "RAND_STATE = 42\n",
        "\n",
        "# Perform t-SNE on textual embeddings\n",
        "tsne_text = TSNE(n_components=3, random_state=RAND_STATE)\n",
        "tsne_feats_text = tsne_text.fit_transform(text_embeds)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Perform t-SNE on concise embeddings\n",
        "tsne_concise = TSNE(n_components=3, random_state=RAND_STATE)\n",
        "tsne_feats_concise = tsne_concise.fit_transform(concise_embeds)\n"
      ]
    },
